### Bug description

A member that joins a consumer group while another member's partitions are still pending revocation gets no partitions, and the group never corrects it.

Setup: one topic with 4 partitions, one consumer group. Member A owns all 4 and has polled them without committing, so they are in flight. Members B and C then join back to back.

Expected: 2, 1, 1.

Actual: A=2, B=2, C=0. This stays the same under continuous traffic  (60 seconds). `consumer-group get` shows the same thing:

```
| Members count       | 3                                           |
| Members             |  Member id | Partitions count | Partitions  |
|                     |  0         | 2                | 0, 1        |
|                     |  1         | 2                | 2, 3        |
|                     |  2         | 0                |             |
```

If C joins after B's revocations have completed, the split is correct (2, 1, 1). With nothing in flight, the split is also correct, because the partitions move at join time.

This is not #3334. That fix spreads excess over several idle members in one rebalance. Here the second join's rebalance does not see B as needing anything and does not see C as owed anything.

### Cause

In `ConsumerGroup::rebalance_cooperative` (core/metadata/src/stm/consumer_group.rs), step 2:

- Partitions pending revocation are subtracted from the source's count, so A counts as owning 2.
- A member that is the target of a pending revocation is left out of the idle list, so B is skipped.

https://github.com/apache/iggy/blob/e4ff95b8852ca0b86efaaa68d62c27d8a2c58fec/core/metadata/src/stm/consumer_group.rs#L229-L254

When C joins, there are 3 members, so fair share is 1 with a remainder of 1. A's effective count of 2 is within `fair_share + 1`, so nothing is collected as excess and C gets nothing. The plan already made for B (two partitions) is not revisited either.

The rebalance only runs on join and leave. `complete_revocation` moves the partition to its recorded target and bumps the generation, but does not rebalance again, so the uneven split is permanent until the next join or leave.

https://github.com/apache/iggy/blob/e4ff95b8852ca0b86efaaa68d62c27d8a2c58fec/core/metadata/src/stm/consumer_group.rs#L321-L363

### Affected area / component

Iggy server

### Deployment

Docker (DockerHub image)

### Versions

server 0.9.0

### Hardware / environment

local Mac laptop

