### Reproduction

Failing integration test, next to `should_timeout_revocation` in core/integration/tests/data_integrity/verify_consumer_group_partition_assignment.rs:

```rust
#[iggy_harness(test_client_transport = [Tcp, WebSocket, Quic], server(
    heartbeat.enabled = true,
    heartbeat.interval = "60s",
    consumer_group.rebalancing_timeout = "3s"
))]
async fn should_balance_member_that_joins_while_revocation_pending(harness: &TestHarness) {
    const PARTITIONS: u32 = 4;
    let root_client = harness.root_client().await.unwrap();

    setup_stream_topic_cg_with_partitions(&root_client, PARTITIONS).await;
    for partition_id in 0..PARTITIONS {
        let message = IggyMessage::from_str(&format!("msg-p{partition_id}")).unwrap();
        let mut messages = vec![message];
        root_client
            .send_messages(
                &Identifier::named(STREAM_NAME).unwrap(),
                &Identifier::named(TOPIC_NAME).unwrap(),
                &Partitioning::partition_id(partition_id),
                &mut messages,
            )
            .await
            .unwrap();
    }

    // 1. Consumer1 joins, gets all 4 partitions and polls each without
    //    committing, so every partition is in flight.
    let client1 = harness.new_client().await.unwrap();
    client1
        .login_user(DEFAULT_ROOT_USERNAME, DEFAULT_ROOT_PASSWORD)
        .await
        .unwrap();
    join_cg(&client1).await;
    let consumer = Consumer::group(Identifier::named(CONSUMER_GROUP_NAME).unwrap());
    for _ in 0..PARTITIONS {
        client1
            .poll_messages(
                &Identifier::named(STREAM_NAME).unwrap(),
                &Identifier::named(TOPIC_NAME).unwrap(),
                None,
                &consumer,
                &PollingStrategy::next(),
                1,
                false,
            )
            .await
            .unwrap();
    }

    // 2. Consumer2 joins: 2 partitions are pending revocation toward it.
    let client2 = harness.new_client().await.unwrap();
    client2
        .login_user(DEFAULT_ROOT_USERNAME, DEFAULT_ROOT_PASSWORD)
        .await
        .unwrap();
    join_cg(&client2).await;

    // 3. Consumer3 joins before those revocations complete.
    let client3 = harness.new_client().await.unwrap();
    client3
        .login_user(DEFAULT_ROOT_USERNAME, DEFAULT_ROOT_PASSWORD)
        .await
        .unwrap();
    join_cg(&client3).await;

    // 4. Wait past the revocation timeout (3s) + check interval (1s) + margin.
    sleep(Duration::from_secs(6)).await;

    // 5. With 4 partitions and 3 members the split must be 2/1/1.
    let cg = get_consumer_group(&root_client).await;
    assert_eq!(cg.members_count, 3);
    assert_unique_partition_assignments(&cg);
    assert_balanced_partition_distribution(&cg, PARTITIONS);

    // Cleanup
    root_client
        .delete_stream(&Identifier::named(STREAM_NAME).unwrap())
        .await
        .unwrap();
}
```

It fails on all three transports, every run (9 of 9):

```
Member 2 has 0 partitions, expected between 1 and 2. Distribution is unbalanced!
Members: [{ id: 0, partitions: [0, 1] }, { id: 1, partitions: [3, 2] }, { id: 2, partitions: [] }]
```

The same steps with the Java SDK 0.9.0 against the apache/iggy:0.9.0 image give the same result. In that run A commits its batch after C joins, so the revocations complete on commit, not on timeout.

Possible fix:
Rebalance again when a revocation completes. After `complete_revocation` moves the partition, run the cooperative pass again. The apply has no in-flight data, so it would treat every owned partition as in flight and pending-revoke the excess. The reconciler already completes a never-polled or drained partition on its next pass, so the cost is one extra tick. This also covers any other case where a pending plan goes stale.

